    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (no rung of the ladder guarantees a value crossing between two representations of one concept is refused unless a row declares it; the wall that decides it is a bare name comparison). CEILING: structurally guaranteed (decidable once the classifier reads the resolved declaration at every position). NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the Map ConversionPlan pair beside unicode_scalar_unfold/fold in gunbc.structural_realization_bindings (the same carrier, not a new mechanism; total because FinitelySupportedFunction is declared as a fn-backed total surface over a finite support and the kernel Map's host map IS that support -- one host operation, v1_rt's map helpers, bound through the *_primitive_delegate seams; exact because the pair's endpoints name the two declarations, never the leaf name); plus an executed RED (undeclared kernel Map <-> FinitelySupportedFunction use refuses with a typed, located diagnostic naming the missing crossing) and a positive control through the declared plan.",
    "FOLLOW-UP (named, not silent; the sibling leaves of the join rule #15118 fixed -- DESIGN 6b, 'consolidate duplicate answers'): seed judgments still key on the leaf spelling Map and must be keyed by declaration identity, each with its own RED that a look-alike leaf named Map does not match. THE CENSUS IS AN IDENTITY JOIN OVER A STATED POPULATION, NOT A COUNT EQUALITY (DESIGN section 5). Review 86783 caught four named against six claimed; review 87351 caught a named site that does not exist and a hand count that was wrong again. So the count is gone and what is stated instead is the POPULATION and its PARTITION, with every figure machine-derived from the population by the derivation given here -- rerun it and the classes recount themselves. POPULATION: the lines of `grep -n` for the token Map inside double quotes over src/v1/*.dag (the command review 86783 cited), which at this head is 18 lines across five files: 04_infer.dag, 04_lookup.dag, 04_types.dag, 04_resolve.dag, 05_emit.dag. PARTITION, each line assigned to exactly one class by its enclosing symbol; disjoint and exhaustive, 6 + 10 + 1 + 1 = 18: CLASS (a), SIX judgments that COMPARE the leaf spelling -- the probes, named below. CLASS (b), TEN uses that SUPPLY the kernel container PROFILE name for Map: three in v1.compiler.infer_types bare_map_node and seven in make_map_type (container_param_name calls, the constructed node name, and the profile-miss diagnostic pair). A profile constructor names the built-in it builds; it is not a judgment over authored text and cannot conflate two representations. CLASS (c), ONE line supplying a rendering fallback base name: v1.compiler.emit emit_map_type (”fallback_base: Map”, src/v1/05_emit.dag). CLASS (d), ONE judgment already keyed on DECLARATION IDENTITY: v1.compiler.infer_resolve container_declaration_aliases_keyed_algebra (src/v1/04_resolve.dag), whose comparison is a declaration_ref_eq against the std.types Map declaration reference. The population grep catches it