ctly where the type name resolves to NOTHING -- unbound_container_diagnostics runs on the kernel-minting path, so there is no resolved declaration node to hand container_declaration_aliases_keyed_algebra -- and the resolve phase sits BELOW the infer phase that resolves references and builds TypeEnv, so no declaration identity exists to compare yet. Its harm direction is the opposite of the other five: a roster line can only REFUSE a name, never RENDER a look-alike as the built-in, so a user-declared type named Map reaching probe 6 is refused rather than conflated. It is still a leaf-name key, still tracked, and its next rung is named: give the resolve phase the declaration answer, and probe 6 stops being a roster question. Each probe carries a RED on this branch or is named here with the reason it does not. The six stay OUT of the crossing branch: six more seed judgment changes would widen the blast radius of a branch that must rebase over the ~110-module Map import wave, so this row is the trigger that keeps them tracked.",



